    '}'
]
  ok the collapsed width is never overridden
  ok viewer content keeps a constant rail gutter
  ok tab labels stay hidden in the rail
  FAIL a hovered tab unfolds its title over the content 
  FAIL the unfolded title opens beside the tab, leaving its icon visible 
  FAIL hovering never hides the tab's icon 
  ok drag/keyboard reordering runs on the vertical axis
3) panel icons lead the rail, tabs follow below them:
  ok the panel action icons render inside the rail
  ok panel icons come before the tab-list chevron
  ok panel icons come before the tabs
  ok nothing is stacked above the panel icons
  ok the spacer drops below the tabs
  ok no "+" add button is left in the rail
  ok the add button component is gone from the app
  ok the rail action container fills the rail width
  ok rail icon buttons share one width
4) every page owns one rail icon, in a fixed order:
  ok the terminal toggle renders in the rail
  ok fill every page icon
  ok fullscreen sits directly below the tab-list chevron
  ok files leads the rest of the page icons
  ok todos sits below files and above artifacts
  ok artifacts follows todos and sits above the terminal
  ok the terminal follows artifacts
  ok schedule follows the terminal, inbox follows schedule
  ok review, trace and browser close the icon list
  ok the rail rows and the tabs come last
  ok the todos page owns a rail icon (not raw markup in App)
  ok the rail button is a plain titlebar icon button
  ok it starts unpressed
  ok its label offers to open the terminal here
  ok the tooltip and the label agree
  ok it paints a stroke glyph instead of a filled app badge
  ok the first press reveals the side pane
  ok it requests the side dock
  ok it opens the terminal
  ok the effective dock really is the pane
  ok pressing it again closes the terminal
  ok a stale side request still opens the terminal
  ok a hidden pane degrades the dock (so the icon reads unpressed)
5) a page icon is pressed only while its page is ON SCREEN:
  ok the icon of the shown page is pressed
  ok …and offers to close it
  ok the icon of an open-but-hidden page is not pressed
  ok …and still offers to open it
